# The Fetch API: Making GET Requests 📡

The `fetch()` function sends HTTP requests to servers and returns a Promise:

```javascript_not
async function fetchUsers() {
  try {
    const response = await fetch("https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users");

    // Check if HTTP status is 200-299
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error(`HTTP Error! Status: ${response.status}`);
    }

    const users = await response.json();
    console.log("Loaded users:", users);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Network or parse error:", error.message);
  }
}

fetchUsers();
```

> ⚠️ **Fetch Gotcha:** A `fetch()` Promise **does not reject** on HTTP 404 or 500 errors! It only rejects on total network failure. You **must check `response.ok`**!

# Sending Data: POST Requests 📤

To create or submit data to an API, pass a configuration object with `method`, `headers`, and `body`:

```javascript_not
async function createPost(newPost) {
  const response = await fetch("https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      "Content-Type": "application/json"
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(newPost) // Must convert object to JSON string!
  });

  const savedPost = await response.json();
  console.log("Created post ID:", savedPost.id);
}

createPost({ title: "Learning Web APIs", body: "Fetch API is clean!", userId: 1 });
```

# HTTP Headers & Bearer Tokens 🛡️

Pass security tokens (like JWT) in the `Authorization` header:

```javascript_not
async function fetchProtectedResource(authToken) {
  const response = await fetch("/api/dashboard", {
    headers: {
      "Authorization": `Bearer ${authToken}`,
      "Accept": "application/json"
    }
  });

  if (response.status === 401) {
    console.warn("Unauthorized! Redirecting to login...");
    return;
  }

  return await response.json();
}
```

# Request Cancellation with `AbortController` 🛑

Cancel ongoing requests if the user navigates away or types a new query:

```javascript_not
const controller = new AbortController();

// Cancel request after 5 seconds timeout
const timeoutId = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 5000);

try {
  const response = await fetch("/api/heavy-report", {
    signal: controller.signal // Link signal to fetch
  });
  const data = await response.json();
} catch (err) {
  if (err.name === "AbortError") {
    console.warn("Fetch was cancelled due to timeout!");
  }
} finally {
  clearTimeout(timeoutId);
}
```

# Mastering `localStorage` 💾

The `localStorage` API provides simple key-value methods:

```javascript_not
// 1. Save data
localStorage.setItem("theme", "dark");
localStorage.setItem("fontSize", "16");

// 2. Read data
const currentTheme = localStorage.getItem("theme");
console.log("Saved theme:", currentTheme); // "dark"

// 3. Remove single item
localStorage.removeItem("fontSize");

// 4. Clear all stored data for this origin
// localStorage.clear();
```

# Storing Objects in `localStorage` 📦

`localStorage` only stores strings! To store arrays or objects, serialize them with `JSON.stringify` and deserialize with `JSON.parse`:

```javascript_not
const userPreferences = {
  theme: "dark",
  volume: 80,
  recentCourses: ["html", "css", "js"]
};

// ❌ WRONG: Stores "[object Object]"!
// localStorage.setItem("prefs", userPreferences);

// ✅ CORRECT: Serialize to JSON string
localStorage.setItem("userPrefs", JSON.stringify(userPreferences));

// Retrieve and parse back into a JavaScript object:
const saved = localStorage.getItem("userPrefs");
const parsedPrefs = saved ? JSON.parse(saved) : null;
console.log("Restored volume:", parsedPrefs?.volume);
```

# Cross-Tab Synchronization with `storage` Event 🔄

When `localStorage` is updated in one browser tab, the `storage` event fires in **all other open tabs** of the same website:

```javascript_not
// Listen for changes made in other tabs
window.addEventListener("storage", (event) => {
  if (event.key === "theme") {
    console.log(`Theme changed from ${event.oldValue} to ${event.newValue} in another tab!`);
    applyTheme(event.newValue);
  }
});
```

Enables instant live synchronization (e.g. logging out in one tab logs out all open tabs!).

# The Geolocation API 📍

The Geolocation API allows web applications to access the user's geographic coordinates (latitude and longitude) with their explicit permission.

```javascript_not
if ("geolocation" in navigator) {
  console.log("Geolocation is supported by this browser.");
} else {
  console.warn("Geolocation is NOT supported.");
}
```

> 🔒 **HTTPS Requirement:** The Geolocation API is strictly restricted to **secure contexts (HTTPS)**! It will be blocked on insecure HTTP sites.

# Getting Current Location (`getCurrentPosition`) 🌍

```javascript_not
function getUserLocation() {
  navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(
    // Success callback
    (position) => {
      const { latitude, longitude, accuracy } = position.coords;
      console.log(`Latitude: ${latitude}, Longitude: ${longitude}`);
      console.log(`Accuracy radius: within ${accuracy} meters`);
    },
    // Error callback
    (error) => {
      switch (error.code) {
        case error.PERMISSION_DENIED:
          console.warn("User denied location permission.");
          break;
        case error.POSITION_UNAVAILABLE:
          console.warn("Location information unavailable.");
          break;
        case error.TIMEOUT:
          console.warn("Location request timed out.");
          break;
      }
    },
    // Options
    {
      enableHighAccuracy: true,
      timeout: 10000,
      maximumAge: 60000 // Cache location for 1 minute
    }
  );
}
```

# Live Location Tracking (`watchPosition`) 🚶

For fitness apps, navigation maps, or tracking real-time movement:

```javascript_not
let watchId = navigator.geolocation.watchPosition(
  (position) => {
    console.log("Moved to:", position.coords.latitude, position.coords.longitude);
  },
  (err) => console.error(err),
  { enableHighAccuracy: true }
);

// To stop tracking when user finishes activity:
// navigator.geolocation.clearWatch(watchId);
```

# The Clipboard API (Copy & Paste) 📋

Read and write directly to the system clipboard:

```javascript_not
// Copy text to clipboard
async function copyToClipboard(text) {
  try {
    await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
    console.log("Copied to clipboard successfully!");
  } catch (err) {
    console.error("Failed to copy:", err);
  }
}

// Paste text from clipboard (requires user permission prompt)
async function readFromClipboard() {
  const text = await navigator.clipboard.readText();
  console.log("Pasted text:", text);
}
```

# Web Notifications API 🔔

Display native operating system notifications to users:

```javascript_not
async function notifyUser(title, message) {
  // 1. Request permission
  const permission = await Notification.requestPermission();

  if (permission === "granted") {
    // 2. Spawn native notification
    new Notification(title, {
      body: message,
      icon: "/images/icon-192.png"
    });
  }
}

notifyUser("Goal Achieved! 🏆", "You earned 100 Knowledge Points today.");
```

# Multi-Tab Communication with `BroadcastChannel` 📢

Broadcast messages directly across all open tabs, windows, and iframes on the same origin:

```javascript_not
const channel = new BroadcastChannel("auth_channel");

// Send logout broadcast
function logoutUser() {
  channel.postMessage({ action: "LOGOUT" });
  performLogout();
}

// Listen in other tabs
channel.onmessage = (event) => {
  if (event.data.action === "LOGOUT") {
    console.log("Logged out from another tab! Redirecting...");
    window.location.reload();
  }
};
```

# Real-World Component: Live Weather Fetcher 🌤️

```javascript_not
async function loadLocalWeather() {
  navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(async (pos) => {
    const { latitude: lat, longitude: lon } = pos.coords;

    // Fetch weather using coordinates
    const url = `https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?latitude=${lat}&longitude=${lon}&current_weather=true`;
    const response = await fetch(url);
    const data = await response.json();

    console.log(`Current Temperature: ${data.current_weather.temperature}°C`);

    // Cache last known weather in localStorage
    localStorage.setItem("cachedWeather", JSON.stringify(data.current_weather));
  });
}
```
